# ============================================================================
# Secrets & credentials
# Patterns are doublestar-matched against the TARGET path (what lands in $HOME),
# NOT the source name: a source file `dot_aws/credentials` is the target
# `.aws/credentials`. Ignoring only stops chezmoi from picking a file up; it
# never un-manages one that is already tracked (use `chezmoi forget` + `git rm`).
# Verify any change with: chezmoi ignored
# ============================================================================
.config/zsh/secrets.zsh
.config/zsh/*secret*
.netrc
.github/credentials*
.aws/credentials
.aws/config
.ssh/id_*
.ssh/known_hosts
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.key
*.pem
*.p12

# ============================================================================
# Repo-only files — documentation and helper binaries belong in the repo, not
# in $HOME. `README.md` at the source root would otherwise deploy to ~/README.md
# and `bin/` to ~/bin (where a 42 MB copy of the chezmoi binary used to sit).
# ============================================================================
README.md
bin/
bin/**

# ============================================================================
# Machine-specific state
# ============================================================================
.local/share/zinit/**/cache/**
.local/state/**
.cache/**

# OS-specific binaries (installed by the bootstrap script / package manager)
.local/bin/*

# Local data managed externally (zinit and fzf are chezmoiexternal targets)
.local/share/**
!.local/share/zinit/**
!.local/share/fzf/**
